  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting a protective environment and ending violence against women and girls in Tripoli and Miniye Donniye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgt


lt/pgtltp style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot; class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;gtltspan style=&quot;line-height: 107% font-family:&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;gtThe
intervention will focus on strengthening the protection environment for GBV
survivors and individuals at risk through GBV prevention activities and
response services in North of Lebanon (Tripoli  Menye Donniye). The intervention will target women and girls, and
individuals at risk from the most marginalized communities, including
vulnerable Lebanese and refugee communities, in addition to migrant
communities, who remain a severely under-served population group at high risk
of violence and exploitation. Survivors with disabilities will also be
prioritized for support, as they face increased restrictions in accessing GBV
services due to physical and societal barriers, and who are at increased risk,
especially considering compounded crises. Access to safe, quality, and
specialized GBV services is a central component of this intervention, in
addition to prevention and risk mitigation activities with GBV survivors,
individuals at risk and their communities. Additional and distinct
considerations will be put in place in reaching and supporting survivors and
individuals at risk from migrant communities, as well as those with
disabilities, to ensure timely, unhindered, and equitable access to project benefits
and services provided.lt/spangtltspan lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;gtlt/spangtlt/pgt





ltp class=&quot;sceditor-nlf&quot;gtltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
